3.17.m:
One seeking food obtains food merely by constantly remembering [her].
The Lord Maheśvara himself attends upon the Narmadā constantly;
therefore the holy river should be known as destroying [even] the murder of a brāhmaṇa.

3.18.m:
Giving a bilva fruit with ghee, and afterwards performing circumambulation,
one should carry it on one's head with the god from all sides;
endowed with all desires, one becomes a king, O Pāṇḍava.
